{{Short description|Central administrative ministries and agencies of Okaiken}}
{{Politics of Okaiken}}

The {{Nihongo|'''Ministries of Okaiken'''|中央省庁|Chūō shōchō|Central ministries and agencies}}, legally designated as the {{Nihongo|administrative organs of the state|行政機関|Gyōsei kikan}}, constitute the primary bureaucratic apparatus within the [[Executive (government)|executive branch]] of the [[Government of Okaiken]]. Each line ministry and statutory cabinet-level organ is directed by a [[Ministers of State (Okaiken)|Minister of State]] nominated by the [[Prime Minister of Okaiken]] and formally invested by the [[Emperor of Okaiken]].

In the contemporary administrative era under the [[Ikazaki Cabinet]], ministerial leadership is shared among the governing coalition partners: the [[Sanese Communist Party]] (SCP), the [[Okaiken Socialist Party]] (OSP), and the [[Social Democratic Party (Okaiken)|Social Democratic Party]] (SDP). While political ministers establish strategic directives and defend legislative policy before the [[National Diet of Okaiken]], extensive administrative management, institutional memory, and statutory enforcement are maintained by career civil servants headed by each ministry's Administrative Vice-Minister (事務次官, ''Jimu Jikan'').

==Statutory architecture and classification==

The organizational structure of the central government is codified under the National Government Organization Act and the Cabinet Office Establishment Act. The central administration is divided into three distinct institutional categories: the overarching Cabinet coordinating apparatus, the eleven statutory line ministries, and specialized cabinet-level regulatory agencies and commissions.

